WEBVTT

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.270
I left Hokkaido to live with my cousin...

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.750
who has been like an older brother
to me since I was little.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.960
I entered Nadesico Academy's
art program...

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.360
when my Onii-chan's childhood
friend suddenly appeared.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.390
Did you kiss?

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.490
Who knows.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.400
Onii-chan, what color is your heart now?

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:05.040
Mischievous Canary Yellow

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.410
Let's see, we bought conditioner.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.030
What else...

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.010
They're handing out balloons.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.650
Elis!

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.780
This is why you're still just a kid.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.290
Is that Hagino?

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.480
Here you go.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.160
Not that one! Give me a
Gloria Blue one instead.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.030
Gloria...

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:41.670
This one!

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.280
Onii-chan.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.350
What are you looking at?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.720
Here, hold this too!

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.910
Come on.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.560
Let's go to the bookstore next.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.590
Elis sure is taking her time.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.550
Their eyes are sparkling.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.310
“Bring on the Love?”

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.240
Who reads this stuff?

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.920
Hagino-senpai.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:22.700
Hagino?

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:23.850
No.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.550
“Nakano Giwa” is Hagino-senpai's
pen name.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.810
She writes novels?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.630
Yeah. She's pretty famous
at the academy.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:34.570
It's not my cup of tea, though.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.900
But enough of that.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.560
You want me to buy all of these?

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.500
Can I get a part time job?

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.320
No.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.720
Then you'll buy them?

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.450
There are some other books
I'm interested in.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.640
I'll go take a look.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:51.030
I should pay for these these now.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.940
That smells amazing. Delicious.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:06.010
We must be having cream stew tonight.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:10.860
Is that Hagino-senpai's book?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.310
The stew is burning!

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.250
Oh, no!

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:36.810
Hey.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.400
Oh, it's you, Sensei.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.730
I'm not a teacher.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.720
No!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.400
Hey, Hagino.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.340
You looked, didn't you?

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.600
Sorry.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.620
Hagino, I didn't know you're
a professional writer.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.450
What did you think?

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.390
I was surprised it was so well written.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.550
It's got good pacing and
your own unique flair.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.330
Hooray!

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:19.030
Oh, stop it. I'm currently accepting
harsh criticisms, too.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.970
I guess I would say it lacks realism.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:26.640
Realism...

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:30.910
Yeah. They're supposedly lost
in the throes of love...

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:34.850
but the characters seem
like they're acting.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.530
But it's great anyway.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.750
I guess this is what you'd
call a girly novel. It's...

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:48.410
It's...

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.890
Afternoon classes are starting.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.360
Yeah.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.540
Yes?

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.070
Thank you for earlier.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:11.980
Sure.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.390
What's wrong, Hagino?

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.340
Stop.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.190
Huh?

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.930
I'm tired of being hurt.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:24.860
What?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.640
Listen, that was just an
amateur's critique...

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.580
It's fine. You were right.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.370
What?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:36.740
I haven't dated a man before.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:37.810
Hagino...

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:43.250
I'm writing romance novels but I
haven't been on a single date.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.330
It's all just fantasy.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.810
Sensei! Please take me
out on my first date!

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:55.630
A date? Why can't you ask
one of your classmates?

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:58.880
You're the one who said my
book lacked realism.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.320
Take responsibility for your words!

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.770
Responsibility...

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.130
Please!

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.570
Fine, I'll do it.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.720
Really?

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:18.320
Hooray! This is fantastic!

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:20.580
Promise, okay?

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.440
Now I've got to find the perfect outfit.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.110
Hey, Hagino...

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.290
I'll let you know when we'll meet later.

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:28.330
Bye!

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.070
Elis, you're still here?

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.400
I bought you a drink.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.870
Oh, thanks.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:41.980
You're going on a date?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.930
Oh, you were listening?

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.240
It might be a date, but I'm sure
she'll just be gathering...

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:50.670
You shook this, didn't you?

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:59.450
Going on a date just because
someone asked him to...

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.090
That jerk!

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:12.520
Sensei, over here!

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.910
You're here early.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:20.530
Yes, a girl in love arrives
twenty minutes early.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:21.600
In love?

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:24.920
A normal date for a normal couple!

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:26.690
I've done all my background research.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.590
Let's go.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:28.420
Sensei!

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.910
That's way too close!

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.950
Elis-chan?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.660
Hiroki isn't with you today?

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.530
No, uh...

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.780
I should get going.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.500
Wait, I'll go with you.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.010
Huh?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.400
You're a detective today, aren't you?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.150
How would you like an
athletic assistant?

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:06.660
Ready...

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.660
Set, go!

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.620
Elis-chan, hurry up!

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.220
We'll lose them!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.550
Kiri-san...

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:38.120
We'll start with a cup of tea at a cafe.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.790
I guess that's pretty standard, but...

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.160
is this really a cafe?

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.730
You mean it's not?

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.480
Welcome home, master.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.780
What can I get you?

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:10.650
What's he doing in a place full of girls?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:13.660
Yes.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.390
What happened to you?
You didn't even call.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.140
Oh, no. Was that today?

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:20.420
What, you forgot?

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.020
I was just in the middle of something.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:22.850
What?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.840
Well, you know...

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:28.430
Is it a guy? I'll forgive you if it's a guy!

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.640
A man's love is greater than
a woman's friendship.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:34.490
Well, it's starting to look
something like that...

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:35.770
so I'll have to cancel today.

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:38.430
Okay. I look forward to
hearing about it later.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.650
Talk to you soon.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.880
She stood me up.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:48.010
I guess I'll have to check on Sensei.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.700
Devil Editor

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:58.760
I cannot come to the phone right now.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:03.140
Oh? I thought she said she'd be
writing at home this weekend.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.880
Don't you need to answer that?

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.580
No, it's fine. Don't worry about it.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.030
I feel like I've seen that cosplay before.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.580
It's Aimi-chan's limited edition
birthday event outfit...

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:25.000
from the game “Sazameki Academy.”

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.940
This is Nadesico Academy's
Hosen Elis' outfit!

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.530
Calm down, Elis-chan!

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.950
Let me get a picture of you.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.380
Look this way, too.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.850
I didn't know about that character.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:45.850
She must be a hidden character.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.550
She's from a new game?

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.890
Apparently, Purikura is a
standard date activity.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.490
It commemorates the outing.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.620
Sure, but...

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:56.890
Tada!

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.360
Do we have to wear costumes?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.010
Of course!

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.360
I'll give you a shot if you're
not a good boy.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.950
Sensei, smile more!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.710
I'm not good at this kind of thing.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.840
That's an interesting idea.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.120
How far will they go for this book?

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.340
Hiroki can't say no.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.020
He's always been that way.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.370
Always...

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:30.580
He's not like that now.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:33.470
I'll ask him for small portions,
but he'll give me tons.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.800
I'll ask him to wash my sweaters
with softener, but...

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.070
Hiroki does the cooking and the laundry?

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:42.020
It's not like I make him do it.

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:44.270
We decide with rock paper scissors.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.390
He's still terrible at rock paper scissors.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.780
He's kind to a fault.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:54.720
He's always trying to please others.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:59.930
Because of that, I can never
tell what he's thinking.

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:00.600
Huh?

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.560
Do you...

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:04.410
Huh?

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:05.660
Oh, no!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.530
When did they get away?

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.540
Onii-chan!

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:12.630
Let's go!

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.310
Miss, your hats! Your hats!

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.430
Next, we'll see a movie.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.990
Let me catch my breath.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:32.320
No. I already checked the movie times.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:33.820
Right now they're showing...

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.860
16 missed calls

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.860
Devil Editor

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:36.790
Oh, no!

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.220
What's wrong, Hagino?

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.370
Sensei, Sensei!

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:46.700
Sensei!

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:49.260
Sensei, let's play tag!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.160
What?

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.300
Did you know playing tag is
a standard date activity?

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:55.350
I've never heard of anyone
doing that on a date.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.140
It's a generational gap.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:01.850
All the high school girls
are doing it these days.

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:03.790
You're it, Sensei!

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:05.680
Come on! This way!

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:06.490
Hey!

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:09.690
Are you okay?

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.470
Sensei! What are you doing?

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:16.930
Is that...

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.410
Sensei,

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:26.480
your manuscript!

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:27.580
Here!

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:28.150
Huh?

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.110
Must be a generational gap.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:33.350
In my day, carrying your date on your
back was a standard date activity!

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:33.950
What?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:35.390
Just hurry up!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:36.820
Okay!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:38.780
Ready?

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:39.340
Yes.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:40.160
Let's go!

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.130
Wait!

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:56.370
All right!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:58.910
Go!

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.180
Bye-bye!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.820
You said you'd be working!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.560
Sensei, everyone's staring.

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.000
Do you want to get down?

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:23.770
No, I'll stay here a little longer.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:26.430
Found you!

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.810
You won't get away!

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:33.840
Kiri-san, you're too fast!

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.900
Wasn't that fun, Sensei?

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:55.960
I'm not a teacher.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:01.170
Who was that woman?

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:06.610
Well, uh...

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:12.050
I've seen you meeting with her before.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:20.140
You looked like you were dying.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:26.930
That woman is my editor.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.580
I'm in a slump.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.270
We finally caught up.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:44.420
What should we do?

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:58.900
I've dreamed of becoming an
author since I was little.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.840
But I'm always being chased
by deadlines...

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:05.430
and forced to do work
I don't want to do.

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:12.370
Gradually I lost sight of what
I wanted to write.

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.250
I want to quit.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.060
Chasing your dreams is rough.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.030
What?

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:38.970
You want to believe it's easier
to let go of your dreams...

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:44.910
but really, it's just the opposite.

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:47.620
Sensei...

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:57.220
Onii-chan...

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:07.430
Why don't you stick with
it a little longer?

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.150
I'll go out with you any time you want...

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.980
but I won't carry you any more.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.300
Thank you, Sensei!

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.780
We should get going.

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:29.630
We can't go yet.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:30.400
Huh?

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:35.890
There's still a special event
to mark the end of a date.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.950
The parting kiss!

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.020
The kiss?

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:46.780
There are twenty kisses
in one of my books!

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.310
I need to experience it at least once
if I want to make it more realistic!

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:52.560
Yeah, but...

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:55.270
Wait, slow down, Hagino!

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:57.250
Sensei, hurry.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.140
I'm not going to...

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.490
No!

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.120
Stop!

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.360
Elis-chan, no!

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:17.070
Hey!

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:24.210
What are you two doing?

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.980
Did you really think we'd do it?

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.590
Hagino-senpai?

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:38.090
Sensei, Elis-chan has been following
us this whole time.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:39.010
Huh?

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:42.190
I didn't expect you to follow
us too, Kiri-sensei.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:44.460
What does that mean?

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.680
Let's see.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:46.890
I not only experienced a date...

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:49.130
but I also had the thrill of being chased.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.050
It was fantastically exciting.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.470
I can feel the creativity
bubbling up inside me.

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.620
Thank you, everyone!

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.410
Hey, Hagino!

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:07.310
Lucky you, Hiroki. You went on
a date with a high schooler.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.930
No, that was...

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.980
And you embarrassed yourself by carrying
her in front of strangers.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.140
That was because...

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:20.830
Thanks for the food!

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:24.270
Hey! Why do you have
to take the main dish?

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:27.440
But you were so generous
with Hagino-senpai.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:31.390
An A lunch is nothing compared
to a cake set.

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:32.530
Right?

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:35.450
How long are you two going
to blackmail me?

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:36.530
Sensei!

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:39.260
It's my new book.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.610
I'm still in the middle of writing...

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:42.820
but I wanted you to be
the first to read it!

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:45.260
Sure, what's it about?

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:49.690
Well, sparks fly between two
girls chasing the same man.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:56.380
I still haven't written the ending yet...

00:20:56.380 --> 00:21:01.030
but a third girl will appear and
steal the heart of the man!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.070
How does that sound?

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.070
Hey...

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:09.100
One fried shrimp...

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.800
One fried chicken...

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:13.650
Won't be enough...

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.710
Hey, wait!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.930
Give us that!

00:23:10.690 --> 00:23:13.240
Cobalt blue is the color of clear skies.

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:18.320
So Onii-chan, why can't men
leave weak girls alone?

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.300
I just want to protect them.

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:22.420
Girls like that are a lot of work.

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:23.580
That's true.

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:25.720
Cheering them up all the
time is a lot of work.

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:29.430
Wouldn't you prefer a girl who
can make it on her own?

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:30.500
I don't know about that.

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:33.510
A strong woman would probably
give me a hard time.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:34.610
Don't be a baby!

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:36.690
Next episode, “Cobalt
Blue Impatience.”

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:39.220
Love is important, but so is friendship!
